---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | BoxBox">
  <main class="relative z-10 min-h-screen bg-[#0d0d0d] text-text-primary px-4 py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <a href="/" class="text-sm text-accent hover:text-white transition-colors">
        ← Back to home
      </a>

      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-white">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-muted">
        Last updated: August 2026
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3">Self-hosted by design</h2>
          <p>
            BoxBox is a self-hosted file manager. When you run it on your own server, all of
            your files, credentials, and activity stay on hardware that <em>you</em> control.
            BoxBox does not phone home, does not collect telemetry, and does not route your data
            through any third-party service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3">Your data stays on your server</h2>
          <p>
            The files you manage, the accounts you configure, and the uploads you make are stored
            and processed entirely on your own BoxBox instance. There is no cloud component, no
            analytics, and no backend operated by the project that sees your content.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3">This website (boxbox.radhey.dev)</h2>
          <p>
            The public project website is hosted on Vercel and served statically. It does not set
            tracking cookies. To show the latest release banner, the site fetches public release
            metadata from the GitHub API; that request is cached server-side and contains no
            personal information about you.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3">GitHub</h2>
          <p>
            Source code, releases, and issue tracking live on GitHub, which is governed by
            GitHub's own privacy and data policies. Anything you post publicly there
            (issues, comments, pull requests) is subject to those policies.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3">Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            This policy may be updated as the project evolves. Material changes will be reflected
            here with an updated revision date.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3">Contact</h2>
          <p>
            For privacy or security questions, open an issue on the
            <a href="https://github.com/jR4dh3y/BoxBox" target="_blank" class="text-accent hover:text-white transition-colors"> GitHub repository</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>